{"title":"KVPY","category":"Engineering","bank":"kvpy","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Hyperbola","count":4,"questions":[{"id":51702,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Hyperbola","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"A mirror in the first quadrant is in the shape of a hyperbola whose equation is $\\mathrm{xy}=1 .$ A light source in the second quadrant emits a beam of light that hits the mirror at the point $(2,1 / 2)$. If the reflected ray is parallel to the $\\mathrm{y}$-axis the slope of the incident beam is","options":["$\\frac{13}{8}$","$\\frac{7}{4}$","$\\frac{15}{8}$","$2$"],"answer":2,"solution":"<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FEmxbLBHxK7lwzEK9vXv5tv1hdjDRVWfgANobb85toEA.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FEmxbLBHxK7lwzEK9vXv5tv1hdjDRVWfgANobb85toEA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FEmxbLBHxK7lwzEK9vXv5tv1hdjDRVWfgANobb85toEA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>\nSlope of tangent at $\\left(2, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\mathrm{m}=-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n\\tan \\theta=-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{y}} \\\\\n\\theta=\\phi-90^{\\circ} \\\\\n\\tan \\theta=4\n\\end{array}\n\nSlope of incident ray $=\\mathrm{m}$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\left|\\frac{m-\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}{1+m\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}\\right|=\\tan \\theta=4 \\\\\n\\left|\\frac{4 m+1}{4-m}\\right|=4 \\\\\n4 m+1=16-4 m \\\\\nm=\\frac{15}{8}\n\\end{array}\n","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2015 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2138b10bd385cd0819c"},{"id":51703,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Hyperbola","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"On a rectangular hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>></mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> three points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>C</mi></math> are taken as follows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo>;</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> are placed symmetrically with respect to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis on the branch of the hyperbola not containing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. Suppose that the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is equilateral. If the side length of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> lies in the interval","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>]</mo></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>]</mo></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>We have rectangular hyperbola</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>\n<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252F9f87c898-f46c-4cd4-b7f8-07e6b5739d3d-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2F9f87c898-f46c-4cd4-b7f8-07e6b5739d3d-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2F9f87c898-f46c-4cd4-b7f8-07e6b5739d3d-image.png?alt=media\"/></p>\n<p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is an equilateral triangle.</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>sec</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo></math> Side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>tan</mi><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>tan</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p>\n<p>But side of triangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></math>.</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p>\n<p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da6a10963f9785ee967a2"},{"id":51704,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Hyperbola","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Suppose $a, b$ are real numbers such that $a b \\neq 0 .$ Which of the following four figures represents the curve $(\\mathrm{y}-a \\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{b})\\left(\\mathrm{bx}^{2}+\\mathrm{ay}^{2}-\\mathrm{ab}\\right)=0 ?$","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FtdYNWgvImI9iC7u1h3oxj_I9oLdUsI_QZIyms750aOE.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FtdYNWgvImI9iC7u1h3oxj_I9oLdUsI_QZIyms750aOE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FtdYNWgvImI9iC7u1h3oxj_I9oLdUsI_QZIyms750aOE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FlyB-UR83yDPrC0cRoxDH_nx1qitYONU3G10zBZmiJqU.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FlyB-UR83yDPrC0cRoxDH_nx1qitYONU3G10zBZmiJqU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FlyB-UR83yDPrC0cRoxDH_nx1qitYONU3G10zBZmiJqU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FkN5K8AbP0DqNLRV5rmSQKtd72uDyek3uPiOrkxW9cCE.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FkN5K8AbP0DqNLRV5rmSQKtd72uDyek3uPiOrkxW9cCE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FkN5K8AbP0DqNLRV5rmSQKtd72uDyek3uPiOrkxW9cCE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FB_W61STzucTlEgY9A2zcrOCdX1efxQ3cMt4L4dfVTQA.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FB_W61STzucTlEgY9A2zcrOCdX1efxQ3cMt4L4dfVTQA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FB_W61STzucTlEgY9A2zcrOCdX1efxQ3cMt4L4dfVTQA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\quad y=a x+b$ and $\\frac{x^{2}}{a}+\\frac{y^{2}}{b}=1$\nslope $=\\mathrm{a}$\nfor the line, $y$ intercept $=b$\nFig. 1 for line $\\rightarrow \\mathrm{a} \\lt  0, \\mathrm{~b}\\gt 0$ hence the other fig. cannot be an ellipse Fig.2 $\\quad \\mathrm{a}\\gt 0, \\mathrm{~b} \\lt  0$ hence the fig. is a hyperbola\nSimilarly you can check rest 2 options","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2010 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21392c832f753c3a4b4"},{"id":51705,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Hyperbola","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The sound of a cannon firing is heard one second later at a position $\\mathrm{B}$ than at position $\\mathrm{A} .$ If the speed of sound is uniform, then","options":[